Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::the_scratch_range_never_touches_a_partition_or_sector_zero`.

The defect: the scratch range is computed one sector too late, so it ends ON the first partition's
first sector instead of just before it. On the VisionFive 2's card that sector is the FAT32 boot sector, and
the write test would overwrite it with a pattern before restoring it.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!e.contains(sector))`, on any table with a used entry
starting at 2 or above and `k == count - 1`.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/partition.rs
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@
             return None;
         }
         let count = if want < gap { want } else { gap };
-        Some((first - count, count))
+        Some((first - count + 1, count))
     }
 }
 
